0,Kolbila language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kolbila_language,"Kolbila is an Adamawa language used in Cameroon and Nigeria.Kolbila is closely related to Samba Leko. It is spoken by fewer than 4,000 speakers in several settlements along the Ngaoundéré-Garoua road in Bantanjé (Bantadje) canton of northwest Cameroon (Sabine Littig 2017).",Kolbila,Niger-Congo
1,"Kolbila Language (KLC) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/klc/,Kolbila is a stable indigenous language of Cameroon. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.,Kolbila,Niger-Congo
2,Kolbila - klc (Niger-Congo) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/klc/,"Kolbila (klc) is part of the Niger-Congo family and Niger-Congo, Atlantic-Congo, Volta-Congo, North, Adamawa-Ubangi, Adamawa, Leko-Nimbari, Leko class.",Kolbila,Niger-Congo
3,Kolbila language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/kolbila_language,"Kolbila is an endangered Central Adamawa language of the Niger-Congo phylum, spoken by approximately 2,000 native speakers in the North Region of Cameroon.",Kolbila,Niger-Congo
